
    ->  What is Domain Requirements? Explain with examples :

        * Domain requirements are the specific needs, rules, and constraints that come from the application
domain (the environment or field where the system will operate).They reflect domain
knowledge — that is, the expertise, standards, or regulations of a particular area
such as banking, healthcare, education, or aviation.

   ->   BENIFITS OF RTM :

-> Completeness Check;
     * Ensures all requirements are implemented and tested — no missing or overlooked functionality.

-> Impact Analysis;
     * When a requirement changes, RTM helps identify which test cases, design elements, or modules are affected.

-> Improved Test Coverage;
     * Ensures every requirement has at least one corresponding test case, leading to thorough validation.

-> Requirement Validation;
     * Confirms that all customer needs are correctly translated into design and testing activities.
